# Local development environment. Copy to `.env` to use it.
#
# `.env` is gitignored and never reaches CI: the deploy reads its environment from the workflow
# files — the per-spec callers pass it down to `deploy-cloudflare.yml` — not from here. These values only change what a local
# `npm run dev` / `npm run build` produces.
#
# Two different mechanisms are in play, and only one of them reads this file:
#
#   - `PUBLIC_SPEC` is read by the app as `import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SPEC` (`src/lib/spec/registry.ts`),
#     which is Astro's `.env`-loaded channel: anything `PUBLIC_`-prefixed here is inlined at build
#     time and exposed to the client.
#   - `SITE_URL` and `BASE_PATH` are read by `astro.config.mjs` from the real process environment
#     (`process.env`), **not** from `.env` — set them in the shell (`SITE_URL=… npm run build`) or
#     leave them to their defaults. The deploy sets them in the workflow `env:` block instead.

# The spec a build defaults to, by registry key (`getSpec`): `windwalker` or `elemental`. Unset it is
# the first registered spec. A key that does not resolve falls back the same way rather than failing,
# so a typo here is silent — `npm run dev` just comes up as the wrong spec.
PUBLIC_SPEC=windwalker

# --- not read from `.env`; listed for reference -----------------------------------------------
# Canonical site URL and path prefix, consumed by `astro.config.mjs`.
#
# Defaults to the Cloudflare Pages domain at its root. There is one such domain per spec's site, and
# the deploy passes the matching one — see `.github/workflows/deploy-cloudflare.yml`:
#   SITE_URL=https://windwalker-analyzer.pages.dev
#   SITE_URL=https://elemental-analyzer.pages.dev
#   BASE_PATH=
#
# GitHub Pages needs both, because a project site is served under `/<repo>/` and an unprefixed build
# 404s every asset:
#   SITE_URL=https://1337lutz.github.io
#   BASE_PATH=/windwalker-analyzer
#
# Moving the site means re-registering the OAuth redirect URI with WarcraftLogs — it matches the
# callback byte for byte, and an unregistered URL fails as `invalid_client`.
